# Plan M9, step 4, the limit: a literal that no number type of the translation holds -- the author's
# `int: 342348523485629384569384` -- has no value the receiver could receive at run time, so the check cannot be
# lowered as the `convert` of a reception; the translation refuses the literal where it stands.  A literal that a wider
# type holds is the run-time refusal: receiver_literal_range.
fn: f () int
    int: 342348523485629384569384
    return: 7
end: f
send: exit(exit_code: f(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
